// Unit 9: Evidence (FRE). Ten lessons sized by NCBE's own fractions for the Evidence questions
// (about one-quarter presentation, one-third relevancy, one-quarter hearsay and confrontation, the rest privileges, policy
// exclusions and writings): relevance and judge/jury (L1), witnesses (L2), impeachment (L3), character/habit/other acts (L4),
// proof and writings (L5), privileges and the polite exclusions (L6), hearsay I (L7), hearsay II: 803 exceptions (L8),
// hearsay III: 804 exceptions (L9), the Confrontation Clause (L10).
// Every rule card carries its rule number as `cite`. Fact patterns are our own; nothing is copied from NCBE or commercial outlines
// (u9-h-615-claims-manager and u9-h-801d1a-deposition were rewritten from scratch after review found them too close to NCBE samples).
// Counts: 28 items carry transfer: true ("new facts, same rule" cold asks), not eight; about 30% of the hypos and argue items have
// the key as the longest option (it was 91% before the 2026-11-02 review).
//
// Provenance: `book` = rule text or Supreme Court opinion read in primary text (FRE at law.cornell.edu, the opinions named in `src`).
// `general` = standard doctrine not re-read in primary text: the marital-communications privilege (holder, survival, joint-crime
// exception), no federal physician-patient privilege, clergy privilege, the collateral-matter doctrine, "need not die" for dying
// declarations, Bruton and Gray, Peña-Rodriguez, Bullcoming, Kovel, Upjohn/Swidler elements as recited, work product (Hickman,
// FRCP 26(b)(3)), the majority view that Rule 407 does not reach a nonparty's remedial measures, and the demonstrative-evidence card.
//
// UNDER REVIEW (status "unsure", never drawn by the Question of the Day or the mocks):
//   - u9-tr-801d1a-version: the amended FRE 801(d)(1)(A). VERIFIED 2026-11-02 in the Supreme Court transmittal (order of April 8, 2026,
//     "frev26_da3i.pdf"): only Rule 801 is amended, effective December 1, 2026 (Rules 609 and 613 are NOT amended by that order), and
//     the text reads "(d)(1) ... the declarant testifies and is subject to cross-examination about a prior statement, and the
//     statement: (A) is inconsistent with the declarant's testimony". Still open for a reviewer: (1) that Congress does not act before
